"help.button" = "Help";
"help.title" = "Help";
"help.kicker" = "Nyheter · Guide";
"help.headline" = "Everything you need, in five minutes.";
"help.lede" = "Nyheter turns your Mac’s screen saver into a calm news board. The app is the remote control. Here is how every part works.";
"help.search" = "Search the help";
"help.contents" = "Contents";
"help.noResults" = "Nothing found. Try another word.";
"help.intro.title" = "What is Nyheter?";
"help.intro.body" = "When your Mac rests, the screen saver shows the latest news – one story at a time, big and easy to read.\n\nThe **Nyheter app** is where you decide everything: which news, how long each story stays, how it looks and what to hide.\n\nEvery change shows up right away in the preview at the top of the app – and in the screen saver.";
"help.start.title" = "Get started";
"help.start.body" = "1. Click **Install the screen saver**.\n2. Open **System Settings › Screen Saver** and choose **Nyheter**.\n3. Want to see it now? Click **Show full screen**. Press any key to leave.\n\nThat’s it. The news updates by itself.";
"help.sources.title" = "Choose your news";
"help.sources.body" = "Go to the **Sources** tab.\n\n• Click **Add source** to add a newspaper or channel, like SVT, BBC or The New York Times.\n• Each source has its own switches, for example **World** or **Sport**. Turn on what you like.\n• Click **Remove** to take a source away. Nyheter remembers its settings, so they come back if you add it again.\n• A small warning sign means that feed isn’t answering right now. It usually fixes itself.\n\nYou only see options for the sources you use.";
"help.order.title" = "Order";
"help.order.body" = "In **Order** you decide how the sources mix.\n\n• **Take turns** – one story from each source, in a round you choose. Add a source twice to see it more often.\n• **In order** – all stories from one source, then the next. Drag the sources into the order you want.\n• **Random** – everything shuffled.\n\n**Maximum per source** stops one source from taking over.";
"help.counter.title" = "The numbers in the corner";
"help.counter.body" = "At the bottom right of each story you see something like **12 / 48**.\n\n• The first number is the story on screen.\n• The second is how many stories are in the round right now.\n\nThe round is the latest fetch, minus what you don’t want: only sources that are turned on, no stories your **Filters** hide, each story once, and at most **Maximum per source** from each source (in **Order**). Some sources also have their own limit in **Sources**.\n\nAfter the last story, the round starts over at 1. Every new fetch rebuilds it, so the second number can change. On the live numbers slides, the counter is hidden.";
"help.time.title" = "Time on screen";
"help.time.body" = "In **Time** you choose how long each story stays.\n\n• Pick a fixed time, for example 15 seconds.\n• Or turn on **Adapt the time to the text length**: long stories stay longer, short ones go faster. You set a minimum and a maximum, so nothing flashes by or gets stuck.";
"help.look.title" = "Themes and layout";
"help.look.body" = "In **Theme** you choose the look – from a light morning paper to glowing green code.\n\n• **Pick a random theme each time the screen saver starts** gives you a surprise every time. Tick the themes you like.\n• **Show upcoming stories in the right column** shows what comes next.\n• **Show headlines only** makes the headline big and hides the extra text.\n• **Show the progress line at the bottom** shows how much time is left for each story.";
"help.filters.title" = "Hide what you don’t want";
"help.filters.body" = "In **Filters** you choose what never to show.\n\n• Type a word, like *football*, and click **Add**. Every story with that word disappears.\n• Want more power? Choose **Regular expression**. Example: *(football|hockey)* hides both words.\n• **Hide whole sections** removes, for example, all culture or sport stories at once.\n• If you read news in more than one language, **Applies to** lets a filter work on just one language.\n\nThe **Log** shows what was hidden and why. The word that caused it is shown in **red**. Click **Open large** to see the whole log in a big window.";
"help.fetched.title" = "What was fetched";
"help.fetched.body" = "The **Fetched** tab lists every story Nyheter downloaded, newest first.\n\n• Tick **Only those shown** to see only the stories the screen saver will show.\n• A number like **#12** shows its place in the line-up.\n• A red filter sign means a filter hid it.\n• Click a story to read it on the newspaper’s website.";
"help.world.title" = "The world right now";
"help.world.body" = "Every few stories, Nyheter can show live numbers – like how many people live on Earth right now. They count up while you watch.\n\nThe numbers are smart estimates from official yearly figures, not exact counts. Choose which ones you want in the **World** tab.";
"help.language.title" = "Language";
"help.language.body" = "Nyheter speaks your Mac’s language automatically. Want another one? Pick it in the **language menu** with the flags.\n\nThe news itself stays in the language of each newspaper.";
"help.clock.title" = "The clock on top";
"help.clock.body" = "macOS shows a big clock over the screen saver. Nyheter can’t remove it, but you can: click **Clock…** and set **Show large clock** to **On Lock Screen** or **Never**.";
"help.clock.body.wallpaper" = "macOS shows a big clock over the screen saver. Nyheter can’t remove it, but you can: click **Clock…**, then **Clock Appearance…**, and set **Show large clock** to **On Lock Screen** or **Never**.";
"help.trouble.title" = "If something looks wrong";
"help.trouble.body" = "• **Only “Fetching news…”?** Check your internet connection and that at least one source is turned on.\n• **A source is not responding?** Wait a while. Newspapers sometimes block too many visits.\n• **Too few stories?** Look at your filters and hidden sections in **Filters**.\n• **The screen saver looks old?** Click **Update the screen saver**.";
"help.about.title" = "About Nyheter";
"help.about.body" = "Nyheter is made by **snowdrop**.\n\nGot an idea, found a bug or just want to say hi? Write to **[contact@gaia.li](mailto:contact@gaia.li)**. Every message is read.";
